  "title": "Shortest delivery tour",
  "kind": "code",
  "language": "cpp",
  "level": 5,
  "statement": "A courier starts at depot 0, must visit every one of the other n - 1 stops exactly once, and come back to depot 0. Travel times can differ by direction (going from i to j may not take as long as going from j to i). Find the shortest possible total travel time.\n\nInput: the first line holds n (1 <= n <= 16). Each of the next n lines holds n integers: the j-th number of line i is d[i][j], the time to go from stop i to stop j (0 <= d[i][j] <= 10^6, d[i][i] = 0). Stops are numbered 0 to n - 1.\nOutput: one line with the minimum total time of a tour 0 -> ... -> 0 that visits every stop exactly once. When n = 1 the answer is 0.\n\nWith n = 16 there are 15! (over 10^12) orders, so trying them all is too slow.\n\nExample\nInput:\n4\n0 10 15 20\n5 0 9 10\n6 13 0 12\n8 8 9 0\nOutput:\n35\n(0 -> 1 -> 3 -> 2 -> 0 takes 10 + 10 + 9 + 6 = 35)",
  "starter_code": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<vector<long long>> d(n, vector<long long>(n));\n    for (auto& row : d)\n        for (auto& x : row) cin >> x;\n    // Print the length of the shortest tour\n}\n",
  "time_limit_ms": 1000,
  "memory_limit_mb": 256,
  "comparator": "trim",
  "timer_seconds": 1800,
